WEBVTT

00:03.390 --> 00:04.560
El Minya!

00:06.320 --> 00:09.260
My, you are merciless, Beatrice-sama.

00:09.260 --> 00:15.490
There is no mercy or restraint left 
anywhere in this world for you!

00:17.090 --> 00:17.870
Oh?

00:20.570 --> 00:23.470
Surely even he can't withstand such power.

00:23.470 --> 00:24.150
No...

00:24.450 --> 00:25.170
He's coming!

00:29.370 --> 00:30.170
Murac!

00:35.890 --> 00:39.220
I'd expect no less of you, Beatrice-sama!

00:39.540 --> 00:45.170
Nice! Good! Wonderful! Pleasing! Acceptable!

00:43.360 --> 00:45.170
You just never shut up, I suppose.

00:45.170 --> 00:48.730
I'm curious to see how long you 
can keep up that confidence.

00:48.730 --> 00:50.270
Five more, I suppose.

00:50.850 --> 00:51.570
Huh?

00:52.410 --> 00:55.070
Magic crystals? Wait, aren't those...

00:55.450 --> 00:58.630
They're essential for bringing back Bubby.

00:58.630 --> 01:01.660
One of these is good for one 
great magic spell, I suppose.

01:01.870 --> 01:04.530
I need to save the last one,

01:04.530 --> 01:06.800
so that means I can use five more big spells.

01:06.800 --> 01:08.270
That's crazy!

01:08.270 --> 01:11.670
I can see why you're Natsuki-san's 
contracted spirit!

01:12.780 --> 01:17.070
As far as Betty is concerned, 
that's a compliment!

01:19.600 --> 01:21.230
Al Minya!

01:25.030 --> 01:26.070
Just kidding.

01:40.490 --> 01:42.720
Very admirable, Gaston.

01:42.720 --> 01:46.040
You've worked so hard for an ordinary man,
coughing up blood and all.

01:46.370 --> 01:47.700
Too bad, though!

01:47.700 --> 01:51.460
You tried your very best, 
but it wasn't enough!

01:52.530 --> 01:54.680
You bastard!

01:54.680 --> 01:56.350
Bennett Mossa.

01:56.350 --> 01:57.880
August Valen.

01:57.880 --> 02:00.270
Carsiff Finrell.

02:01.260 --> 02:02.440
Damn it!

02:13.840 --> 02:15.070
Beatrice-chan!

02:15.070 --> 02:18.720
The people who've fallen are allies, 
but I don't know their names!

02:18.720 --> 02:20.340
That's good enough for now!

02:20.340 --> 02:21.170
You little...

02:24.460 --> 02:26.420
Ul Minya!

02:29.250 --> 02:30.970
What a lavish feast!

02:30.970 --> 02:35.470
Impressive, Beatrice-sama!
Are you impersonating Roswaal-sama?

02:35.470 --> 02:39.300
Now, that's just not nice! 
What an insult, I suppose!

02:42.840 --> 02:44.060
Did that get him?!

02:49.060 --> 02:50.390
Shamac!

02:55.270 --> 02:58.200
Not bad, Beatrice-sama!

02:58.200 --> 03:00.910
This is the strength that lies in numbers!

03:01.580 --> 03:04.070
Sorry to keep you morons waiting!

03:04.070 --> 03:09.180
Here you go! Something that'd 
make even Reinhard cry!

03:11.010 --> 03:11.970
How's that?!

03:14.740 --> 03:17.880
That would make the Sword Saint cry?

03:18.990 --> 03:20.140
You must be joking.

03:20.890 --> 03:22.010
Felt-sama!

03:23.290 --> 03:25.270
Felt-chan...

03:26.550 --> 03:28.810
I'll enjoy this treat.

03:51.820 --> 03:53.040
Get ready, I suppose.

03:53.640 --> 03:55.680
You're using it wrong.

04:20.680 --> 04:21.910
Blow to bits!

04:35.470 --> 04:37.680
Now that's power...

04:39.710 --> 04:41.140
Mother...

04:41.140 --> 04:43.250
Beatrice-chan! Felt-sama!

04:43.250 --> 04:44.340
You're all right?!

04:44.340 --> 04:48.460
Yeah! Shorty here showing me how 
to use this thing saved the day!

04:48.460 --> 04:50.010
Who are you calling Shorty, I suppose?!

04:50.860 --> 04:53.820
I just happened to see something 
I had old memories with.

05:08.490 --> 05:09.410
Look out!

05:23.930 --> 05:27.510
You know, having such a useless older brother

05:27.510 --> 05:30.650
makes a little sister's life pretty rough.

05:31.300 --> 05:33.100
Who the hell are you?!

05:33.100 --> 05:36.600
What's this? You're the one asking that?

05:36.600 --> 05:41.570
After a dirty trick like using 
a fake name in front of us?

05:41.570 --> 05:44.200
Fake name? What are you talking about?

05:44.680 --> 05:48.160
Sin Archbishop of... Gluttony?

05:48.160 --> 05:51.360
Oh, wow! You can still speak?

05:51.360 --> 05:55.130
That's amazing, bro!
You're a hard worker, bro!

05:56.850 --> 05:57.710
Nice!

05:57.710 --> 06:02.110
Nice! Lovely! Great! Splendid! Agreeable!

06:02.110 --> 06:03.300
And that is precisely why...

06:03.300 --> 06:08.640
we see the value in letting 
you sit at the table.

06:15.400 --> 06:19.520
Sin Archbishop in the Witch's 
Cult representing Gluttony,

06:19.520 --> 06:20.950
Rui Arneb.

06:20.950 --> 06:25.060
What the hell kind of stupid 
joke are you trying to pull?

06:25.060 --> 06:28.000
What's this? The princess with the fake name

06:28.000 --> 06:30.960
does not find such things to her liking?

06:30.960 --> 06:33.260
Drop the "fake name" bullshit!

06:33.260 --> 06:37.250
I've gone by "Felt," the name that
Old Man Rom gave me, for fifteen years!

06:37.250 --> 06:39.200
Oh, I see.

06:39.200 --> 06:42.310
You don't even realize it's a fake name.

06:42.310 --> 06:45.740
All right, then. Your name is not Felt.

06:45.740 --> 06:49.980
You have another name, a real name,
that you had before the one you have now.

06:50.320 --> 06:53.930
Oh, the name those shitbags who 
dumped me in the alley gave me?

06:53.930 --> 06:57.650
I bet it's something like 
"Nuisance" or "Garbage," right?

06:57.650 --> 07:00.940
Now, there's no need to be so on edge.

07:00.940 --> 07:03.910
We'll be backing off for today.

07:03.910 --> 07:05.740
Do you mean that?

07:06.040 --> 07:10.900
Big Bro just got beaten to a pulp, and 
Elder Brother just does as that woman says.

07:10.900 --> 07:15.750
Whether you're a gourmand or a 
foul feeder doesn't even matter.

07:15.750 --> 07:18.520
They just don't get it.

07:18.520 --> 07:21.100
A meal isn't about what you eat.

07:21.100 --> 07:23.730
It's about who you eat it with.

07:23.730 --> 07:24.640
You...

07:25.500 --> 07:27.520
Dynas Trasaldi.

07:27.520 --> 07:28.470
Gaston.

07:30.780 --> 07:33.350
What'll it be? Want to continue fighting?

07:34.000 --> 07:36.810
Or will you just let this go?

07:41.240 --> 07:44.320
How sad for me that you're so smart!

07:44.320 --> 07:46.820
But you've chosen well!

07:46.820 --> 07:47.970
Damn it!

07:47.970 --> 07:51.700
Forget her. Treating Otto and 
the others is our priority now.

07:52.070 --> 07:53.730
We can settle the score after that.

07:53.730 --> 07:55.870
<i>People of Priestella!</i>

07:56.170 --> 07:58.070
<i>The four control towers have been reclaimed,</i>

07:58.070 --> 08:02.270
<i>and the Witch Cultists who were threatening 
the town have been driven back!</i>

08:02.270 --> 08:04.980
<i>The city's safety has been secured!</i>

08:04.980 --> 08:08.540
<i>The Watergate City Priestella is victorious!</i>

08:08.540 --> 08:10.430
That was the end of it?

08:10.430 --> 08:12.470
I can't even be happy about this, damn it!

08:13.880 --> 08:15.090
Subaru...

08:18.390 --> 08:20.390
Subaru, is this...

08:20.390 --> 08:23.310
It didn't look like this when I left.

08:23.590 --> 08:25.670
What happened?

08:25.670 --> 08:27.650
So you're finally back, I suppose.

08:28.110 --> 08:30.440
I was getting tired of waiting for you two.

08:31.150 --> 08:31.900
Beako!

08:31.900 --> 08:33.230
Beatrice!

08:33.230 --> 08:35.460
Should you be up and about?!

08:35.460 --> 08:38.530
You used up your mana and went 
sleepy-bye at the worst time!

08:38.530 --> 08:42.770
Could you not say it in a way that 
places the blame on me, I suppose?

08:42.770 --> 08:46.370
It's because of Betty's devotion 
that your legs are intact!

08:46.370 --> 08:48.540
This isn't nearly enough 
gratitude or hugs, I suppose!

08:49.620 --> 08:50.880
I know.

08:51.280 --> 08:52.960
I know that!

08:53.320 --> 08:56.520
You had to work so hard 
while I was away again.

08:56.520 --> 08:59.520
Sorry I'm always causing you so much trouble.

08:59.520 --> 09:02.970
It's a given that you're 
going to cause trouble for me.

09:02.970 --> 09:05.070
You don't need to worry about that.

09:05.070 --> 09:07.670
Emilia, I'm relieved to see 
you're also well, I suppose.

09:07.670 --> 09:10.360
Bubby would be sad if 
anything happened to you.

09:10.690 --> 09:12.470
Yeah, you're right.

09:12.470 --> 09:14.940
Thank you for worrying about me, too.

09:15.230 --> 09:15.940
Hmph!

09:16.880 --> 09:18.950
So... where's everyone else?

09:19.310 --> 09:22.380
Looks like they really went to town here.

09:22.380 --> 09:24.370
No need to worry 'bout that.

09:24.370 --> 09:28.320
It's a long story, but it 
was all part of the plan.

09:28.320 --> 09:29.920
Anastasia-san.

09:29.920 --> 09:33.220
In any case, I'm glad you 
two are doin' all right.

09:33.220 --> 09:36.380
And you really can be a boy 
after all, Natsuki-kun.

09:36.380 --> 09:38.370
Yes, Subaru is a boy.

09:38.370 --> 09:40.760
I'm not sure what kind 
of valuation that is...

09:41.140 --> 09:43.470
Anyway, is everyone else okay?

09:43.470 --> 09:46.050
Everyone's back safe an' sound.

09:46.050 --> 09:48.930
None lost. We won!

09:50.360 --> 09:52.190
I knew ya could do it, boss!

09:52.500 --> 09:56.120
Way to show what a man you 
are, savin' Emilia-sama!

09:56.120 --> 09:57.340
Naturally!

09:57.340 --> 09:59.830
What about you, though? Are you okay?

09:59.830 --> 10:02.050
You're all beat up, and you look like hell.

10:02.050 --> 10:05.120
I don't wanna hear comments 
on my looks comin' from you.

10:07.890 --> 10:11.830
I'm glad you seem to be feeling 
much better than you look.

10:11.830 --> 10:13.710
Too much better, I suppose!

10:13.710 --> 10:16.630
He's nice and quiet when he 
actually acts like he's wounded.

10:16.630 --> 10:18.760
Hey! Garf, there you are!

10:18.760 --> 10:21.020
Bam-bammity-bam!

10:21.800 --> 10:25.340
Damn it, don't go trompin' all over me!

10:25.990 --> 10:27.930
Milady told me somethin'!

10:27.930 --> 10:31.510
That you're s'posed to... dominate men,
or somethin' like that!

10:31.510 --> 10:33.500
So I'm tryin' that!

10:33.500 --> 10:34.690
Good grief.

10:35.100 --> 10:39.020
Like Beatrice-chan said, you should 
really act like a man who's hurt.

10:36.860 --> 10:39.020
Carelessness is your greatest enemy, Garf!

10:39.020 --> 10:41.090
The true enemy lies within you!

10:39.020 --> 10:41.090
Hey, Otto, you're here, too?

10:41.090 --> 10:43.570
I've been here the whole time! 
Could you be more shameless?!

10:43.570 --> 10:46.790
Oh, no, Garf! My wound opened up again!

10:43.570 --> 10:46.790
Otto-kun, how are your injuries?

10:46.790 --> 10:48.820
Look at all the blood!

10:46.790 --> 10:50.120
I'll probably have trouble 
walking for a while,

10:48.820 --> 10:50.770
Idiot! What did I tell you?!

10:50.120 --> 10:51.750
but I think they'll heal.

10:50.770 --> 10:52.670
C'mere! I'll fix you up!

10:52.670 --> 10:53.530
Owie!

10:53.530 --> 10:56.750
Beako told me everything,
Mr. Militant Internal Affairs Officer.

10:56.750 --> 10:59.510
Talk to me before you leap 
into danger, would you?

10:59.510 --> 11:00.970
We're friends, aren't we?

11:00.970 --> 11:02.810
And put even more on your shoulders

11:02.810 --> 11:07.590
when you were already dealing with 
Emilia-sama's abduction and the fate of the city?

11:07.590 --> 11:11.770
I'm never going to dump a weight 
that heavy on a friend's back.

11:11.770 --> 11:14.770
Man, you really do play dirty, you know that?

11:15.530 --> 11:18.480
I'm sorry to say that Gluttony got away.

11:20.120 --> 11:23.070
But that doesn't mean we 
gained nothing from this.

11:23.070 --> 11:23.820
What?

11:24.310 --> 11:28.170
Priscilla-sama has captured 
one of the Sin Archbishops.

11:33.420 --> 11:36.480
So you've come to see me, my dear!

11:36.480 --> 11:38.630
I'm sorry about this. Thank you.

11:40.610 --> 11:43.290
Spirit in the shape of a woman!

11:43.290 --> 11:46.470
Stay away from my darling Petelgeuse!

11:46.470 --> 11:50.610
You really feel like you're in a 
position to snap at her right now?

11:50.610 --> 11:54.280
Subaru, it's a waste of time 
to expect repentance or empathy

11:54.280 --> 11:57.110
from a person so lacking 
in humanity, I suppose.

11:57.530 --> 12:00.570
If you feel you're in danger, 
I'll step in right away.

12:01.680 --> 12:04.110
I'm the one you'll be talking to,
just like you wanted.

12:04.110 --> 12:06.990
And just so you know,
no one's coming to save you.

12:06.990 --> 12:10.020
All your buddies either 
got killed or retreated.

12:10.020 --> 12:12.850
Oh, I don't expect anyone to save me.

12:12.850 --> 12:16.210
Saying something so obvious 
to hide your shyness.

12:16.530 --> 12:20.300
You truly are adorable, my dear!

12:22.140 --> 12:24.610
What is it you guys are after?

12:24.610 --> 12:26.330
Why would you all collectively demand

12:26.330 --> 12:29.710
the Tome of Wisdom and the 
artificial spirit and all that?

12:29.710 --> 12:31.310
What were you all after?

12:31.780 --> 12:35.820
I don't even care to know what 
those others were thinking,

12:35.820 --> 12:39.750
but we gathered in this city on 
instructions from the Gospel.

12:39.750 --> 12:42.140
The Gospel again?

12:42.140 --> 12:45.270
Why would you do whatever some book says?

12:45.270 --> 12:49.280
Because it'll help you guys revive 
your beloved Witch of Envy?

12:49.750 --> 12:52.040
Please don't get the wrong idea.

12:52.040 --> 12:53.370
The wrong idea?

12:54.030 --> 12:56.820
The only one I love is you, my dear.

12:56.820 --> 12:59.030
You and no one else.

12:59.030 --> 13:02.710
I couldn't possibly care less 
about the Witch of Envy.

13:02.710 --> 13:07.680
Everything I did, I did because it 
was necessary in order to reach you!

13:08.230 --> 13:10.210
Couldn't care less?

13:10.210 --> 13:11.850
What about the others?

13:11.850 --> 13:14.810
What were you guys hoping 
to achieve in the end?

13:14.810 --> 13:17.060
I don't know. I'm sorry.

13:17.060 --> 13:20.940
I don't know because the only 
thing I'm interested in is you!

13:22.880 --> 13:26.190
You're overwhelmed, aren't you?

13:26.190 --> 13:31.080
Because you simply can't 
live without me, my dear!

13:38.630 --> 13:40.300
Don't try anything funny.

13:40.300 --> 13:43.590
I'm a clumsy girl, so I'm 
not good at holding back!

13:43.590 --> 13:45.800
It's pointless to continue talking to her.

13:46.040 --> 13:47.490
Y-Yeah...

13:48.300 --> 13:51.780
Still the morning comes...

13:51.780 --> 13:55.310
The blue sky always overtakes the dawn...

14:03.070 --> 14:07.190
Stop it! What are you trying to do?

14:08.570 --> 14:10.650
I said stop it!

14:13.090 --> 14:16.530
I'm sorry. But singing 
is wonderful, isn't it?

14:16.530 --> 14:18.600
I just learned that recently.

14:18.600 --> 14:21.910
Don't talk about your singing and 
Liliana's like they're the same!

14:21.910 --> 14:24.080
Yours is a totally different thing.

14:24.080 --> 14:26.390
I could say the same to you.

14:26.390 --> 14:27.380
What?

14:27.380 --> 14:30.320
Petelgeuse is inside you.

14:30.320 --> 14:32.550
Your soul and his have melded together,

14:32.550 --> 14:35.590
and your flesh and his are combined.

14:35.590 --> 14:36.470
So...

14:36.870 --> 14:40.340
I will drag him out from inside you.

14:40.340 --> 14:43.920
I will witness his awakening 
from closer than anyone else!

14:44.370 --> 14:46.780
Thank you. I'm sorry.

14:46.780 --> 14:50.650
Please take care of your body and 
mind until that day comes, won't you?

14:50.650 --> 14:52.880
Subaru, we're leaving, I suppose.

14:52.880 --> 14:55.110
This woman is nothing but a danger.

14:55.110 --> 14:56.350
R-Right.

14:56.350 --> 14:58.490
If I may give you just one warning...

14:59.660 --> 15:01.870
Beware of Gluttony.

15:01.870 --> 15:05.050
Gourmand, Foul Feeding, and Satiation

15:05.050 --> 15:07.510
will all attempt to take you away.

15:11.170 --> 15:14.260
See? Nothing to gain from that at all.

15:14.260 --> 15:16.620
All it did was make you feel gross, right?

15:16.620 --> 15:19.050
Don't just assume we came back empty-handed.

15:19.050 --> 15:21.430
It's not like we didn't get 
anything out of her at all.

15:21.780 --> 15:23.400
Oh, really?

15:23.400 --> 15:26.370
You sure do know how to make 
those freaks like you, huh?

15:26.370 --> 15:28.780
Don't make it sound so creepy.

15:28.780 --> 15:31.530
Subaru, don't go getting 
too friendly with them.

15:31.530 --> 15:33.630
Aw, don't be so cold.

15:33.630 --> 15:36.070
Didn't I help wake you up, Beako?

15:36.070 --> 15:40.100
Subaru is the only person Betty 
allows to call her that, I suppose.

15:40.100 --> 15:41.660
Oh, good grief.

15:41.990 --> 15:45.670
Al, thank you for giving Subaru my message.

15:47.540 --> 15:48.370
Sure.

15:49.160 --> 15:51.170
I'm glad you're doing good, too.

15:52.230 --> 15:55.640
What's up, Beako?
Something happen between you and Al?

15:56.180 --> 16:00.040
It's this. He brought it, I suppose.

16:00.040 --> 16:02.850
This is what got me to wake up.

16:03.570 --> 16:07.060
Kiritaka's magic crystal? How did he...

16:07.320 --> 16:09.030
I don't know, I suppose.

16:09.030 --> 16:12.600
And he has told me not to ask about it.

16:12.600 --> 16:15.870
What the heck was Al plotting 
on his own, anyway?

16:15.870 --> 16:17.200
That's way too shady.

16:17.200 --> 16:20.510
I don't think Al is a bad guy, though.

16:20.510 --> 16:21.910
Emilia-tan...

16:21.910 --> 16:24.700
I mean, it's thanks to 
him that Beatrice woke up

16:24.700 --> 16:27.080
and Otto-kun's team was saved, right?

16:27.080 --> 16:31.170
He found the magic crystal that we 
would've been lost without. Right?

16:31.600 --> 16:33.380
Grr, I suppose!

16:33.380 --> 16:37.060
Man, I'm no match for you, Emilia-tan.

16:39.180 --> 16:42.570
I'm opposed to lettin' 
that Sin Archbishop live.

16:42.570 --> 16:44.350
Nothin' good will come of it.

16:44.820 --> 16:48.010
But then we'll lose our lead 
on how to save Crusch-sama!

16:48.010 --> 16:54.610
Do ya honestly think we'll get anything 
useful on Gluttony or Lust out of Wrath?

16:54.610 --> 16:57.030
But that's just speculation!

16:57.030 --> 16:57.950
Personally...

16:57.950 --> 17:02.660
I don't think talking to Wrath 
would be a total waste of effort.

17:02.660 --> 17:06.870
But I get why you're uneasy 
about keeping her in custody.

17:06.870 --> 17:10.250
That's so noncommittal!
Whose side are you on, anyway?!

17:10.250 --> 17:14.250
All I'm saying is we shouldn't 
rush to a decision.

17:14.250 --> 17:14.960
Ferris.

17:15.310 --> 17:16.820
Sit.

17:16.820 --> 17:19.310
First of all, Subaru-dono is correct.

17:19.310 --> 17:21.810
I know! I know that!

17:21.810 --> 17:24.650
I'm also opposed to the execution of Wrath.

17:24.650 --> 17:26.930
Aside from Crusch-sama's condition,

17:26.930 --> 17:30.660
this is a rare opportunity for the 
kingdom to learn about the Witch's Cult.

17:30.660 --> 17:34.320
We should transport her to the capital 
and give her to the knights at once.

17:34.750 --> 17:36.720
You're not worried she'll escape?

17:36.720 --> 17:39.190
It won't be easy to escort a Sin Archbishop!

17:39.190 --> 17:40.910
I will assume that role.

17:41.890 --> 17:44.550
If Reinhard's going, I'm going, too.

17:44.550 --> 17:47.120
We'll get her to the capital safely.

17:47.120 --> 17:49.630
You can't complain about 
that, right, cat-ears?

17:50.920 --> 17:54.440
That just leaves what to do with the 
fly folks and the nameless folks,

17:54.440 --> 17:58.280
and in particular, Lust's victims.

17:58.280 --> 18:00.340
Even I can't heal them.

18:00.340 --> 18:03.920
No... It's not even about whether 
they can be healed or not.

18:03.920 --> 18:06.850
Creatures like them have 
been completely remade.

18:06.850 --> 18:12.800
I'm sure the ones who were turned 
into disgusting bugs wish for death.

18:12.800 --> 18:16.180
If there is no hope of returning 
them to their original forms,

18:16.180 --> 18:18.160
that would be the merciful thing to do.

18:18.160 --> 18:19.430
Priscilla, that's—

18:19.430 --> 18:20.710
Quiet, peasant.

18:20.710 --> 18:23.580
Ideals that are all talk have no value.

18:23.580 --> 18:27.380
Wait! Could you let me 
take care of that problem?

18:27.380 --> 18:30.710
How amusing. And what could a half-devil do?

18:31.100 --> 18:33.500
I can't heal them right away,

18:33.500 --> 18:37.300
but I think I can buy time 
to look for a way to do so...

18:38.060 --> 18:39.760
by putting them to sleep in ice.

18:39.760 --> 18:42.110
Oh, yeah! Cold sleep!

18:42.110 --> 18:44.310
That would definitely buy us time!

18:44.720 --> 18:46.790
Put them to sleep in ice?

18:46.790 --> 18:48.390
Is that safe?

18:48.390 --> 18:51.690
It's not gonna just freeze 'em to death?

18:51.690 --> 18:53.510
No need to worry!

18:53.510 --> 18:55.940
Emilia-sama doesn't make mistakes!

18:55.940 --> 18:57.830
And that's because...

18:57.830 --> 19:02.780
the greatest people in history are the 
ones who overcome trials such as these!

19:02.780 --> 19:06.230
Those are certainly big words, songstress.

19:06.230 --> 19:09.560
And what if, perchance, your 
estimation proves wrong?

19:09.560 --> 19:12.630
If it does, I'll offer up my own head!

19:12.630 --> 19:15.840
Liliana never goes back on her word!

19:16.570 --> 19:17.610
Fine.

19:17.610 --> 19:19.590
Out of respect for the songstress's warbling,

19:19.590 --> 19:22.180
I shall entrust you with my compassion.

19:22.180 --> 19:25.820
You can trust me. I will make it work.

19:26.640 --> 19:29.630
Hmph. See that you do.

19:29.630 --> 19:33.760
Once you do, I will 
acknowledge you as my rival.

19:35.040 --> 19:44.410
<i>A new morning paints the sky in red-gold</i>

19:44.910 --> 19:56.820
<i>Quietly, as if yesterday's hustle 
and bustle is forgotten</i>

19:48.070 --> 19:53.790
I cannot thank you enough for all 
that you've done to protect our city.

19:53.790 --> 19:56.820
I'm happy to accept your gratitude,

19:56.820 --> 19:58.550
and I'm glad you came out 
of it all right, too.

19:59.080 --> 20:02.330
I was fully prepared to die.

20:02.330 --> 20:03.510
But...

20:04.300 --> 20:08.430
Remembering Liliana's song 
somehow kept me alive.

20:14.300 --> 20:24.070
<i>A new day begins, chasing away the night</i>

20:24.070 --> 20:35.140
<i>Overtaking the red-gold dawn</i>

20:35.140 --> 20:43.590
<i>The true morning comes at last</i>

20:46.300 --> 20:52.140
<i>As the sky overtakes the dawn</i>

20:52.140 --> 20:57.030
<i>No matter what the night may bring</i>

20:57.030 --> 21:05.180
<i>Even if I'm tortured by an unwanted dream</i>

21:05.180 --> 21:11.840
<i>Still the morning comes</i>

21:11.840 --> 21:16.900
<i>It comes to all of us</i>

21:16.900 --> 21:17.970
Subaru.

21:17.970 --> 21:19.630
Oh, Reinhard.

21:17.970 --> 21:29.090
<i>The blue sky always overtakes the dawn</i>

21:20.060 --> 21:23.630
I might not have been able 
to save Emilia without you.

21:23.940 --> 21:27.760
Let me thank you again. Thanks, really.

21:27.760 --> 21:29.090
To help you—

21:31.420 --> 21:34.560
To help a friend was a tremendous honor.

21:34.930 --> 21:37.910
Thank you for lithening!

21:44.990 --> 21:48.920
We'll just have to wait a bit longer 
to see each other again, Puck.

21:48.920 --> 21:51.880
Which we owe to all of Beako's hard work

21:51.880 --> 21:55.000
and the favor Kiritaka showed us.

21:55.000 --> 21:57.940
And you and everyone else, too.

22:00.120 --> 22:02.670
Hey, Subaru. Look over there.

22:03.870 --> 22:05.050
Isn't that...

22:05.050 --> 22:07.260
Lusbel and Tina!

22:07.260 --> 22:12.080
I almost forgot this all started 
with us trying to save them.

22:12.080 --> 22:14.460
I'm so glad they're both all right.

22:14.460 --> 22:16.940
After the town ended up like this,

22:16.940 --> 22:20.980
it might be imprudent to only 
be glad those two are safe...

22:21.330 --> 22:23.650
No, we have to rejoice in that.

22:23.650 --> 22:29.020
Because you and I and all the others 
worked hard to make that happen.

22:29.020 --> 22:29.950
True.

22:34.590 --> 22:35.710
Ricardo!

22:36.830 --> 22:39.600
Hey, bro! You're all right, too?

22:39.600 --> 22:41.300
Hey, your arm...

22:41.300 --> 22:43.330
Oh, yeah. I got a little careless.

22:43.330 --> 22:45.220
I see...

22:45.220 --> 22:49.210
But it's basically a miracle 
I only lost one arm!

22:49.210 --> 22:51.180
Don't worry too much about it!

22:51.870 --> 22:52.890
Yeah?

22:53.200 --> 22:54.420
Sure...

22:54.420 --> 22:56.350
By the way, where's Julius?

22:56.630 --> 23:00.690
Oh, you're right there!
C'mon, don't worry me like that!

23:00.690 --> 23:02.650
Hey, you jerk!

23:02.650 --> 23:06.870
What're you doing just wandering 
around when we're all so busy here?

23:06.870 --> 23:07.900
Julius!

23:08.450 --> 23:11.270
You gotta show your face or 
I'm gonna worry about you.

23:11.270 --> 23:13.590
I mean, that's how everyone feels in general!

23:16.320 --> 23:19.580
Subaru, you... know who I am?

23:19.990 --> 23:20.850
Huh?

23:20.850 --> 23:23.650
What is it, Subaru? Were you busy?

23:23.650 --> 23:26.600
Oh, Julius is acting weird.

23:47.150 --> 23:48.810
Julius-san, are you...

23:50.540 --> 23:52.950
a friend of Subaru's?

23:53.520 --> 23:54.410
Huh?

23:54.910 --> 23:59.870
<b>The Result of the Battle for Priestella</b>
